# Gemini Notebook: Quant Literature Verification

The user has a Gemini Notebook containing 22 specialist quant-finance books
(de Prado AFML, Bailey, Masters, Vince, Carver, Kaufman, Chan, Ehlers, etc.).
The agent may draft a prompt for the user to paste into that notebook to
extract authoritative formulas, algorithms, and caveats BEFORE implementing or
modifying any quantitative method.

## When to use it

- Implementing or changing any formula/algorithm (sizing, risk, execution
  costs, CV/purging, PBO/DSR, Monte Carlo protocols, bar construction).
- Resolving ambiguity between secondary sources or cross-reference critiques.
- Auditing an existing module for subtle bias (look-ahead, selection,
  overfitting).

## How to use it

- Prompts must fit ~3,900 characters: ask for exact equations, algorithm
  steps, and explicit warnings (e.g., de Prado's "c_t stays external to K_t").
- After implementing, record verification status in the module docstring:
  mark formulas as "notebook-verified" vs "not covered by the notebook —
  implemented from <canonical source>" (see `analytics/dsr.py`,
  `execution/costs.py`, `montecarlo/permutation.py` for the pattern).
- Already notebook-verified in this repo: ETF trick + external c_t,
  label-overlap purging/embargo/CPCV counts, CSCV/PBO rank-logit, Masters
  p-value + Trend/Bias/Skill partition, Vince HPR/TWR/f*, TIB & imbalance
  bars, triple-barrier meta-labeling, Carver cost drag + 0.08 SR/yr limit.
